    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe locality derivation now prefers the postcode over the city.\n\n**`Locality.java`** \u2014 added a postcode-first resolution:\n- New `of(String postcode, String city)`: resolves the region from the postcode range first (`NSW 2000-2099`, `VIC 3000-3099`, `QLD 4000-4099`), and only falls back to the existing city-to-region table when the postcode is absent, malformed, or in no known range.\n- The original `of(String city)` city-table lookup is retained (still used by `Postcode.validate`, which must validate a postcode *against its city's* region \u2014 so it correctly keeps using the city path rather than the new postcode-derived one).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `locality` mapping now calls `Locality.of(owner.getPostcode(), owner.getCity())`.\n\n**Behavior:** known cities return the same region (their postcode falls in the matching range), while cities sharing a name are disambiguated by postcode. An unknown city with a VIC-range postcode now yields `VIC`.\n\n**Tests:** the full Maven suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including both existing acceptance tests \u2014 `coreRegionFromPostcodeRange` and `functionalityPostcodePreferredOverCity` \u2014 which already encoded the postcode-first expectation.",
