    "probe_text": "`POST /api/owners` is handled entirely by the OfficeFloor YAML pipeline in `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` (the OfficeFloor starter is present in `pom.xml`, and there is no `@RestController` in `src/main`). Here is everything that runs, in order.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n0. **Authorization** \u2014 `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`; caller lacking the role is rejected before the pipeline starts.\n\nA DB **transaction** governs every step from step 3 (`uniqueIdentity`) through the response, committing once at the end.\n\n## Step-by-step\n\nThe body binds to `OwnerFieldsDto` **without `@Valid`**, so the DTO's jakarta constraints (`@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size`, `@Email`, etc.) are **not enforced by the framework** \u2014 all validation below is done manually.\n\n1. **`RequireOwnerFields`** \u2014 Side-effects + validation:\n   - *Normalizes* the address (trim, collapse whitespace, uppercase, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`).\n   - Validates `firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone` are non-blank \u2192 else `MissingFieldsException` (**400**) listing the offending fields.\n   - *Normalizes* `telephone` to E.164 (`OwnerTelephone.toE164`: strips separators, defaults to `+61`, drops leading `0`; requires 8\u201315 digits, `+61`\u21d29 national, `+1`\u21d210) \u2192 else `InvalidTelephoneException` (**400**).\n   - *Normalizes* `email` (trim + lowercase; blank\u21d2null; must match email regex) \u2192 else `InvalidEmailException` (**400**).\n2. **`RequirePostcode`** \u2014 validates postcode if present: 4 digits and within region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown region accepts any 4-digit) \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException` (**400**).\n3. **`RequireUniqueIdentity`** *(txn)* \u2014 scans `findAll()` and compares contact key (normalized telephone + `|` + normalized email); on match throws `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**).\n4. **`RequireCityCapacity`** *(txn)* \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive/trimmed); if \u2265 50 throws `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n5. **`RequireDailyRegistrationLimit`** *(txn)* \u2014 computes the effective registration date (supplied date or today, weekend rolled forward to Monday); counts owners with that `registrationDate`; if \u2265 100 throws `DailyRegistrationLimitException` (**429**).\n6. **`BuildOwner`** *(txn)* \u2014 maps DTO\u2192`Owner` (ignoring `id`/`pets`) and sets `registrationDate` to the adjusted business day. *(first side-effect that constructs the entity)*\n7. **`AssignCustomerCode`** *(txn)* \u2014 sets `customerCode = <CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN is per-city count + 1.\n8. **`CountNamesakes`** *(txn)* \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n9. **`CountHouseholdMembers`** *(txn)* \u2014 sets `householdSize` = existing owners sharing `Household.id(lastName, address)`, + 1.\n10. **`FlagBulkSignupWarning`** *(txn)* \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = (sameDayCount > 80)`.\n11. **`SaveOwner`** *(txn)* \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 the only persistence call.\n12. **`AuditOwnerCreated`** *(txn)* \u2014 logs `id/customerCode/registrationDate/membershipLevel` to the `AUDIT` logger (after save, so `id` is populated).\n13. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** *(txn)* \u2014 maps to response DTO (enriched with derived `displayName, initials, householdId, identityKey, membershipNumber, membershipLevel, locality, contactPreference`) and returns **201 Created** with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header; the transaction commits.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n- **The DTO's bean-validation annotations are dead** on this path because the handler binds `@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` without `@Valid` \u2014 the pipeline re-implements those checks by hand.\n- The `Owner` entity's own constraints (`@NotEmpty` on names/address/city, telephone E.164 `@Pattern`) only fire if Hibernate Bean Validation runs at persist time; by then the manual steps have already guaranteed those values.\n- `sharesHousehold` from the request is **never consulted** by this pipeline.\n- The active `OwnerRepository` implementation (JPA / Spring Data / JDBC) is chosen by Spring profile, so `findAll()`/`save()` cost varies."
